                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Great old-shool Adventure Game, I played first at my friends house. Yeah the graphics are not fancy by modern standards, the sound is not 5.1 surround and you can really count the pixels on the screen. But you know what? The game makes a lot of fun to me. The puzzles are challenging, the black humor makes me smile and I get that nostalgic feeling while playing of the old Amiga days.\n\nTo mention: The puzzles are getting more and more difficult during the game, sometimes\na little crazy but never unfair. I also loved the entertaining characters\n\"A salute to the honkifant!\". On the con side: Some dialogue cannot be skipped and the controls can be a bit fiddly sometimes. Room for improvement here!\n\nSo to sum up:\n\npros:\n\n+ graphics & sounds give you that pure early 90s feeling\n+ great evil humor\n+ challeging puzzles\n+ funny characters\n+ English & German Audio\n\ncons:\n\n+ some dialogues can't be skipped\n+ maybe quite difficult puzzles for beginners of the genre \n\nverdict:\n\nFor 7,99 really a awesome funny little Adventure-Game I really enjoyed, not just for retro-fans.",
